smartinit.v4.0.0  Q2FY17 

October 2016 NAM/DGEX smartinit changes to coincide with NAM/DGEX_v4 upgrade (see docs/README for more details on changes)

* SMARTINIT and SMARTPRECIP were converted to read and write GRIB2 and will coincide with the NAM/DGEX_v4 upgrade.

* Need grib_util/v1.0.3 installed to use the new wgrib2. Once that is done, you can remove the sorc/wgrib2 directory and 
  remove the local version of WGRIB2 from jobs/JNAM_SMINIT and jobs/JDGEX_SMINIT.

* Need /nwprod/util/sorc/overdateg2.fd installed in util_shared on phase2.  Once it is installed, 
  then replace /nwprod/util/exec/overdateg2 in ush/smartinit_g2.sh with the correct location or command.

* Twelve GRIB2 *wexp files were added to the output directory:

  nam.t${cyc}z.smartconus2p5${hh}.tm00_wexp.grib2

#===============================================================================
 IMPLEMENTATION INSTRUCTIONS 
#===============================================================================
1.  svn checkout https://svnemc.ncep.noaa.gov/projects/smartinit/tags/RB-v4.0.0 smartinit.v4.0.0

    to set up and run on WCOSS phase 2.

2.  Build sorc codes smartinit_g2.fd, smartprecip_g2.fd, smartinit_cnvgrib.fd, and wgrib2
       
	The modulefile used for the build is in modulefiles/SMARTINIT/v4.0.0.  Copy it to a location from which it can
	be loaded (/nwprod2/modulefiles/SMARTINIT or something similar). 

	In the smartinit sorc directory "smartinit.v4.0.0/sorc" type
		./build_smartinit.scr
	to compile the codes sequentially.  All executables will be copied over to the smartinit "exec" directory.

4.  Use ...docs/smartinit.ver file if desired to set
      model_ver=v4.0.0  parameter

5.  My .../ecf subdirectory is different then NCO's .../ecf subdirectory.  I did not try to reconcile it because I do
    not use the ecf subdirectory.  New suggested LSF settings (for the parallel wgrib2):

#BSUB -J DNG06.conusnest2p5-57
#BSUB -oo /ptmpp2/Annette.Gibbs/smartinit.v4.0.0/20161028/06/list/oDNG06.conusnest2p5-57
#BSUB -eo /ptmpp2/Annette.Gibbs/smartinit.v4.0.0/20161028/06/list/oDNG06.conusnest2p5-57
#BSUB -n 12
#BSUB -W 2:00
#BSUB -P RTMA-T2O
#BSUB -q dev2
#BSUB -R span[ptile=12]
#BSUB -R affinity[core(1)]
#BSUB -x
#BSUB -a poe

6.  Job Dependencies: 
     Upstream: NAM/NAM Nest, SREF, GEFS, DGEX; 
     Upstream links:

     NAM/NAM Nest (new locations?)
     /com2/nam/prod/nam.$PDY/nam.t${cyc}z.bgrd3d${hh}.tm00
     /com2/nam/prod/nam.$PDY/nam.t${cyc}z.priconest.bsmart${hh}.tm00
     /com2/nam/prod/nam.$PDY/nam.t${cyc}z.hawaiinest.bsmart${hh}.tm00
     /com2/nam/prod/nam.$PDY/nam.t${cyc}z.conusnest.bsmart${hh}.tm00
     /com2/nam/prod/nam.$PDY/nam.t${cyc}z.alaskanest.bsmart${hh}.tm00

     SREF
     /com2/sref/prod/sref.$PDY/${hh}/ensprod/sref.t${hh}z.pgrb212.prob_3hrly
     /com2/sref/prod/sref.$PDY/${hh}/ensprod/sref.t${hh}z.pgrb243.prob_3hrly
     /com2/sref/prod/sref.$PDY/${hh}/ensprod/sref.t${hh}z.pgrb216.prob_3hrly

     GEFS
     /com2/sref/prod/sref.$PDY/ensprod_gefs/${hh}/sref.t${hh}z.pgrb212.prob_3hrly
     /com2/sref/prod/sref.$PDY/ensprod_gefs/${hh}/sref.t${hh}z.pgrb216.prob_3hrly

     DGEX (new locations?)
     /com2/dgex/prod/dgex.$PDY/dgex_conus.t${cyc}z.bsmart${hh}.tm00
     /com2/dgex/prod/dgex.$PDY/dgex_alaska.t${cyc}z.bsmart${hh}.tm00

     Downstream: RTMA, URMA
     Downstream links(J-Jobs that use NAM smartinit files): 

     /nwprod/rtma2p5.v2.4.4/jobs/J${MODEL}_GETGUESS with MODEL=RTMA2P5, AKRTMA, HIRTMA, PRRTMA
     /nwprod/urma2p5.v2.4.4/jobs/J${MODEL}_GETGUESS with MODEL=URMA2P5, AKURMA, HIURMA, PRURMA

7.  Test plan: 

	Test J-Jobs jobs/JNAM_SMINIT and jobs/JDGEX_SMINIT for a full 24-hour period.

8.  Technical Details:
	Runtime: ~3 hours, 30 minutes wallclock
	Nodes: 12
	Tasks per node: 12
	Consumable memory: 4916 mb
	Serial vs parallel: Parallel (wgrib2 only)
	Disk Storage: Has increased by 0.5 GB total

7.  New output files:

    Twelve GRIB2 wexp files are added to output directory for each cycle, for use in RTMA/URMA:

    nam.t${cyc}z.smartconus2p5${hh}.tm00_wexp.grib2

    where

    ${cyc} = cycle (00, 06, 12, and 18)
    ${hh} = hour (00-12)

8.  Flow Diagram:

    https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B7IqRnJWIYHlbHNjTHFRNWNnNkE

NOTE: Details on all changes to nam smartinit are found at docs/README - Search for 4.0.0 for changes related to this implemenation.

